course: dictionary
lesson: 12929
title: Evasive
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When someone is evasive, they do not answer clearly or directly. They dodge the question, often because they are hiding something. You can spot an evasive answer by asking yourself: did they actually tell me what I asked? «When Sam was asked where the biscuits had gone, he gave an evasive answer and stared at his shoes.» Sam did not say yes or no, so his answer was evasive.
explain: Evasive can also mean a quick movement to avoid danger. «The cyclist took evasive action and swerved round the hole in the road.» The cyclist did not stop to think. She moved fast to get out of the way.
explain: Look at the words around evasive for clues. Words like «answer», «asked» and «hiding» point to dodging the truth. Words like «swerved», «danger» and «crash» point to moving quickly to stay safe. The context tells you which meaning the author means.
fact: Evasive is an adjective, so it describes a person, an answer or an action.
fact: The forms are evasive, more evasive and most evasive.
fact: «Evasive» means avoiding a clear, direct answer, often because you are hiding something.
fact: «Evasive action» means a quick movement to avoid danger, such as swerving or ducking.
fact: «Be evasive about» means to dodge questions about something, as in «The minister was evasive about the cost of the bridge».
exercise: «When asked where the biscuits had gone, Sam gave an evasive answer and stared at his shoes.» What does evasive mean here? | Very loud and cheerful | Quick and kind | Wet and muddy | *Avoiding a clear answer
exercise: «The cyclist took evasive action and swerved round the hole in the road.» Find and copy the word that tells you the cyclist moved quickly to avoid danger. | *evasive | cyclist | hole | road
exercise: «The minister was evasive about the cost of the new bridge.» What does this sentence suggest? | The minister was singing a song | The bridge cost very little | The minister loved building bridges | *The minister did not give a clear answer about the cost
test: «The fox made evasive moves, zigzagging between the trees to escape the hunter.» What are evasive moves? | Loud barks to call its friends | Moves made on a stage | *Quick moves to avoid danger | Slow, sleepy steps
test: If someone is evasive about where they were last night, what are they doing? | *Avoiding a clear, direct answer | Shouting for help | Telling everything in great detail | Singing a happy song
exam: Which sentence uses evasive in the right way? | The evasive cake was delicious and warm | *She gave an evasive answer when asked who broke the window | The evasive dog barked at the postman all day | He ran evasive down the hill to see the view
